{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140395-spirit-sphere-and-what-it-can-do","id":1140395,"title":"Spirit Sphere and what it can do.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-14T19:23:54-07:00","id":1140395,"title":"Spirit Sphere and what it can do.","content":"I'm trying to understand the nature of the Spirit Sphere. For instance, what can it create without drawing on other Spheres, minis prime of course. For instance, do you need Matter to create ephemeral soil or even a rock spirit? Do you need Mind and Matter to transform an Umbral blight into a Glen? Do you need Prime to transform a Web into a Wylding? And what about altering a spirits traits like Gnosis, Rage, and Willpower? Do I need to simultaneously have mastery of the Mind Sphere to use something equivalent to Malleable Spirit from W:tA?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T23:37:06-07:00","id":1140435,"title":"","content":"To create Ephemera on the other side of the Gauntlet, I'm sure you merely need the Spirit sphere - it probably works directly analog to the Matter sphere on the mundane side. Including transformations. Also, that means that at least according to the Mage20 FAQ, the ephemerial object will vanish when the duration ends (just like with matter) unless a point of Quintessence is invested.<br /> And as you mentioned, it can probably work like Life 3/4/5 on Spirits, changing their attributes or form.<br /> Likewise, the creation of Spirits themselves with Sphere 5 does probably not require any other sphere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T11:41:07-07:00","id":1140574,"title":"","content":"Spirits are a lot more than there forms, though. They might look like an owl, an imp, or swirling light but there essence is completely different and this is reflected in their charms. The essence of places in the Umbra is also different. A wylding is a place of creation, and you can probably learn to control the Prime Sphere simply by observing it and its spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theony